OL,3,GNEWSAAI machine 'helps save 25 million
OL,4,ALego bricks'
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn artificial intelligence-powered
OL,7,Fsorting machine has helped save 25
OL,8,Fmillion Lego bricks from landfill, a
OL,9,Fcompany has said.
OL,11,FWeBuyBricks, based at Hall Carr Mill in
OL,12,FRawtenstall, Lancashire, buys unwanted
OL,13,FLego before cleaning and sorting the
OL,14,Fpieces so they can be sold again.
OL,16,FIts Brick-O-Matic uses cameras,
OL,17,Fartificial intelligence and jets of air
OL,18,Fto identify individual pieces and has
OL,19,Fcapacity to sort up to 100,000 of them
OL,20,Fa day, according the to the firm.
OL,23,APub: 17-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
